# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# This project ships hand-written JavaScript and Python with no build step, so
# what is committed is exactly what runs. Letting Git rewrite line endings on
# checkout means a Windows contributor and a Linux contributor diff the whole
# file against each other, and a CRLF in the client bundle is a change nobody
# asked for.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows launchers are the one exception: a .cmd with LF-only endings can
# misbehave under some shells, so they keep CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be text-normalised or diffed.
*.webm binary
*.mp3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
